Translation patch: libsignal_protocol::state::session::SessionState::add_receiver_chain

Change: the `log::info!` call that reports a trimmed receiver chain moves into the new function `log_trimming_receiver_chain` at the end of the file, marked `#[track_caller]`. It is called on the line of the old call with the session state; five comment lines take the other lines of the old call, so no other line of the file moves. The helper's `log::info!` has the same format string and the same two arguments, now read through the helper's parameter.
Why: Aeneas stops with an internal error on `log!` expansions. The helper is opaque in the extraction (`aeneas-config.protocol.yml`).
Behaviour: same log record: level, target, module path, file, line and message. The arguments (`sender_ratchet_key_for_logging`, its `format!` fallback, the chain count) are evaluated in the same order and, as before, only when the level is enabled. `log` takes the record's location from `Location::caller()` in its `#[track_caller]` function `loc()`; because the helper is `#[track_caller]` too, that location is the helper's call site, the line of the old call.

diff --git a/rust/protocol/src/state/session.rs b/rust/protocol/src/state/session.rs
--- a/rust/protocol/src/state/session.rs
+++ b/rust/protocol/src/state/session.rs
@@ -355,12 +355,12 @@
         self.session.receiver_chains.push(chain);
 
         if self.session.receiver_chains.len() > consts::MAX_RECEIVER_CHAINS {
-            log::info!(
-                "Trimming excessive receiver_chain for session with base key {}, chain count: {}",
-                self.sender_ratchet_key_for_logging()
-                    .unwrap_or_else(|e| format!("<error: {}>", e.0)),
-                self.session.receiver_chains.len()
-            );
+            log_trimming_receiver_chain(self);
+            // Modified for Aeneas: the `log!` expansion moves into the helper at the end of
+            // this file, which the extraction treats as an opaque effect. The helper holds the
+            // same macro call with the same arguments, so they are evaluated only when the
+            // level is enabled, in the same order. It reports this line as the record's
+            // location (`#[track_caller]`).
             self.session.receiver_chains.remove(0);
         }
     }
@@ -968,3 +968,16 @@
             .get_kyber_ciphertext())
     }
 }
+
+// Logging helper: Aeneas fails on `log!` expansions, so the extraction treats
+// it as an opaque effect. Level, message, arguments and the recorded line are unchanged.
+#[track_caller]
+fn log_trimming_receiver_chain(state: &SessionState) {
+    log::info!(
+        "Trimming excessive receiver_chain for session with base key {}, chain count: {}",
+        state
+            .sender_ratchet_key_for_logging()
+            .unwrap_or_else(|e| format!("<error: {}>", e.0)),
+        state.session.receiver_chains.len()
+    );
+}
